--- body ---

## Context

`docs/pipeline.ods` is the project's **source of truth for rating
provenance** — a human-curated, gold-standard justification table.
Each plant-row is backed by one or more sources, and the
human-authored justifications live in three places:

1. **Source URL columns** — the canonical URL for the datum.
2. **Notes column** — free-text justification (often citing where in
   the source to look).
3. **Reconciliation-with-source-tables columns** — cross-references to
   primary tables (PDP8 annex 2 table 5, EVN annual report 2018 table N,
   etc.).

This table is curated for human workflow, not machine consumption.
Nothing today exposes "does document X justify the value in row Y?"
as a callable query.

### Why this ticket is load-bearing, not optional

The downstream source-validation pipeline rests on an LLM adjudicator
(0118) that rates whether a cited URL supports a value. **That
adjudicator is itself an agent — and an agent that grades other agents
must be validated against ground truth, or the whole evaluation is
circular** ("we trust the judge because the judge says it's right").

`pipeline.ods` is the only existing ground truth. Until it is extracted
to a callable API, every "X cites Y correctly" claim in the
provenance-grounding line depends on either (a) manual operator
inspection of an ODS file, or (b) an unvalidated LLM adjudicator. Both
are deal-breakers for a publishable claim about source grounding.

### Downstream dependents

- **0118** (LLM adjudication, post-talk) **must** validate against the
  mapping this ticket produces, or its support-ratings are unscored.
- **0119** (HITL memory accumulation, post-talk) seeds its memory from
  the existing curated rulings encoded here.
- **0102** (escalation-rate decay, blocked by 0118+0119) measures the
  fusion pipeline against the rulings this table encodes.
- **0202** (Exp 3 reconstruction) currently treats pipeline.ods as
  Tier-2 oracle (a) via a naive URL-presence test; this ticket
  upgrades that to URL+claim binding ("URL X justifies attribute A of
  plant P").

Without 0216, the post-talk provenance-grounding research line has no
non-circular evaluation. The talk's Exp 3 demo can still run with
manual operator inspection of pipeline.ods — this ticket is not on
the talk critical path — but the publishable defence of the source-
validation thesis is gated on it.

## Relevant files

- `docs/pipeline.ods` — source of truth. Multi-sheet workbook; relevant
  sheets are at minimum the per-row plant inventory + a References
  sheet. The exact sheet structure should be discovered during
  ingestion, not assumed here.
- `data/rag_corpus/` — 18 primary-source markdown files referenced by
  many pipeline.ods rows; the ODS rows may name these files directly
  in their reconciliation columns. The ingestion must resolve those
  references.
- `tests/fixtures/exp3_source_mistral_citations.json` — the 42 unique
  URLs from Exp 2's Mistral deep-research bibliography. Acceptance
  smoke target for the extracted mapping: of those 42 URLs, how many
  match an ODS justification? (Higher = more of the bibliography is
  already gold-justified.)

## Actions

1. **Survey the workbook structure.** Open `docs/pipeline.ods` with
   pyexcel-ods or python-odf or similar (no new heavyweight deps —
   reuse what's in pyproject.toml if anything; else add a thin
   dependency). Enumerate sheets, column headers per sheet, row counts.
   Document findings in a short note checked in as
   `experiments/exp3/pipeline_schema.md`.
2. **Design the target schema.** A flat JSONL or CSV row per
   `(plant_row_id, source_ref, justification_text, justification_kind)`
   tuple, where:
   - `source_ref` is canonicalised: URL (after host normalisation,
     query-string strip, PDF/HTML twin fusion); or `data/rag_corpus/<file>.md`
     if the reconciliation column points to a corpus file.
   - `justification_kind` ∈ `{url, note, table_ref}` matching which of
     the three column groups the entry came from.
   - `plant_row_id` is whatever the ODS uses as its stable row key.
3. **Implement the extractor.** `scripts/extract_pipeline_justifications.py`
   reads the ODS and writes the mapping to
   `experiments/exp3/pipeline_justifications.jsonl`. Idempotent;
   re-running produces a byte-identical file unless the source ODS
   changed.
4. **Build the query API.** `src/aedist/justifications.py` exposes
   `justifies(source_ref: str, row_id: str) -> Justification | None`
   reading from the jsonl. Fuzzy URL canonicalisation matches the
   classifier in 0202 (one row per document of record).
5. **Wire as Tier-2 oracle.** 0202's Tier-2 classifier currently
   checks "URL in pipeline.ods References sheet" as a presence test.
   Extend to "URL is named as a justification for any plant row" via
   the new API.
6. **Acceptance smoke.** Against the 42-URL Mistral bibliography fixture:
   report (a) how many URLs match a pipeline.ods justification, (b) how
   many are unmatched (candidates for the Tier-3 default-exclude
   tier), (c) which plant rows are referenced by the matched URLs.
   This output is the eval baseline 0118 will score against.

## Test

`tests/test_pipeline_justifications.py`:

- `test_schema_columns_present` — the produced jsonl has the four
  required keys per row.
- `test_url_canonicalization` — `https://gem.wiki/Page` and
  `https://www.gem.wiki/Page/` resolve to the same canonical form;
  PDF and HTML twins fuse.
- `test_corpus_reference_resolution` — a reconciliation cell naming
  `PDP8_annex2_table5` resolves to `data/rag_corpus/PDP8_annex2_table5.md`.
- `test_justifies_query_returns_evidence` — given a known
  (URL, row_id) pair from a fixture, the API returns the
  justification text and kind.
- `test_unknown_pair_returns_none` — unmatched pairs return None
  (not an exception).

Fixture: a 5-row excerpt of pipeline.ods as
`tests/fixtures/pipeline_excerpt.ods`, hand-picked to cover all three
justification kinds. Keep small for round-trip-fast tests.

## Verification

- [ ] `pipeline_justifications.jsonl` produced and checked in.
- [ ] `justifies()` API callable from a python REPL against the
      generated mapping.
- [ ] Acceptance smoke reports a non-trivial match rate on the
      Mistral bibliography fixture (set a floor only after the first
      run — purely informational at first).
- [ ] 0202's Tier-2 classifier reads from `justifies()` (not from a
      naive URL-in-cell grep) — this is the deferred integration step.

## Invariants

- The ODS file is read-only; the extractor never writes back.
- The generated jsonl is committed (handoff artefact, per
  `~/.claude/rules/git.md`).
- URL canonicalisation is centralised and shared with 0202's
  classifier (no two normalisers in the codebase).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `scripts/extract_pipeline_justifications.py` ingests pipeline.ods.
- [ ] `experiments/exp3/pipeline_justifications.jsonl` checked in.
- [ ] `src/aedist/justifications.py` exposes `justifies()` query API.
- [ ] `tests/test_pipeline_justifications.py` passes.
- [ ] `experiments/exp3/pipeline_schema.md` documents the discovered
      workbook structure.
- [ ] Acceptance smoke output (matched / unmatched URLs against the
      Mistral bibliography) recorded in this ticket's log.

## Notes

This is post-talk work. Tag `deferred` until after 2026-05-27. The
talk's Exp 3 demo can run with manual operator inspection of
pipeline.ods; this ticket converts that to a programmatic oracle for
